
ESP32-S3-Basic Project README

Overview
- ESP-IDF + PlatformIO project for ESP32-S3.
- Hosts a local web dashboard for:
	- Wi-Fi/device status
	- WS2812 LED control
	- Multi-servo control through PCA9685
- Includes quick per-servo tiny self-tests designed to be gentle on linkages.

Current Feature Set
- Wi-Fi manager with retry and alternate-network fallback.
- Web server with dynamic dashboard and JSON API endpoints.
- LED panel:
	- Color select: red, green, blue, off
	- Auto-off timer after 60 seconds for active colors
- Servo panel:
	- Servo 1..4 controls
	- Angle range: 0..180 per servo
	- Default servo startup angle: 0
	- On dashboard load/refresh: all servos are forced to 0
	- Tiny self-test button per servo: 0 -> 45 -> 0

Servo Channel Mapping
- Servo 1 -> PCA9685 channel 0
- Servo 2 -> PCA9685 channel 1
- Servo 3 -> PCA9685 channel 2
- Servo 4 -> PCA9685 channel 3

Power And Wiring (Important)
- PCA9685 logic power:
	- VCC -> ESP32-S3 3.3V
- PCA9685 servo power:
	- V+ -> external 5V supply
- I2C bus:
	- SDA -> ESP32 GPIO 8
	- SCL -> ESP32 GPIO 9
- Grounding:
	- ESP32 GND, PCA9685 GND, and external 5V GND must be common
- OE (output enable):
	- Keep OE low/enabled on PCA9685

Runtime startup logs include power sanity hints:
- VCC=3.3V logic
- V+=external 5V servo rail
- Common ground requirement

Web API Endpoints

1) Device status
- GET /api/status
- Response example:
	{"connected":true,"ssid":"MyWiFi","ip":"192.168.1.5"}

2) LED control
- GET /api/led?color=red
- GET /api/led?color=green
- GET /api/led?color=blue
- GET /api/led?color=off
- Behavior:
	- red/green/blue start auto-off timer (60s)
	- off disables timer and turns LED off immediately

3) Servo angle control
- GET /api/servo?servo=1&angle=0
- GET /api/servo?servo=2&angle=90
- GET /api/servo?servo=3&angle=180
- GET /api/servo?servo=4&angle=45
- Validation:
	- servo must be 1..4
	- angle must be 0..180

4) Per-servo tiny self-test
- GET /api/servo/sweep?servo=1
- GET /api/servo/sweep?servo=2
- GET /api/servo/sweep?servo=3
- GET /api/servo/sweep?servo=4
- Motion profile:
	- 0 -> 45 -> 0

Build and Flash

Build:
	pio run -e esp32-s3-devkitm-1

Upload:
	pio run -e esp32-s3-devkitm-1 -t upload --upload-port COM5

Serial monitor:
	pio device monitor -b 115200 -p COM5

Project Structure (high level)
- src/main.cpp
	- Starts Wi-Fi manager and web server
- components/wifimanager/
	- Wi-Fi connect logic and reconnection handling
- components/webserver/
	- Dashboard HTML
	- HTTP endpoints for status/LED/servo/tiny self-test
- components/ledmanager/
	- WS2812 LED driver via RMT
- components/servomanager/
	- PCA9685 I2C driver and angle-to-PWM conversion

Notes
- The dashboard served by firmware is compiled from the embedded HTML header in components/webserver/index_html.hpp.
- Keep components/webserver/index.html and components/webserver/index_html.hpp aligned when editing UI.
- If servos do not move, check external 5V servo supply quality and common grounding first.
